Negative luck is as bad as negative alignment for prayer, so that's 
probably why.

Enlightenment also tells you if you can pray - it will say "you can safely 
pray" or "you can not safely pray" or something similar near the bottom.

The other possibility is prayer timeout. Getting a gift from your god 
counts as a prayer.

> Is
> sacrificing the only way, then, to mollify the gods?

AFAIK, yes.

> And if so, what can
> you do until you find a coaligned altar?

Convert a cross-aligned one by sacrificing on it. This is safe provided you 
have positive alignment (luck is not important) and avoid sacrificing 
unicorns coaligned with yourself or the altar and members of your own race 
if you are not chaotic (all IIRC). According to posts here, you can also 
sacrifice a (corpse of a) pet on a cross-aligned altar to mollify your god, 
but I can't personally verify this. I do know sacrificing corpses of pets 
on a coaligned altar is a bad idea, which is a good enough reason to (C)all 
every pet you acquire a name.

Most of this info can be found in prayer spoilers. See e.g.:

http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/pray.html


